== Found while measuring AC4: a gene with a figure that no card can reach ==
The table holds six genes; the capability registry has six primary genes, and they are not the same six. NUDT15 has a
measured figure (78/601, 13.0% [10.5, 15.9]) but is no drug's primary gene, so no card shows it. It is not an
irrelevant gene: backend/app/data/capabilities.json lists NUDT15 among azathioprine's relevant_genes and
evidence_dependencies, and that drug's own limitation says a complete interpretation needs acceptable evidence for
both TPMT and NUDT15. So the azathioprine card shows TPMT's 3.3% and withholds the higher NUDT15 figure for the same
drug. Warfarin is the same shape in the other direction: VKORC1 and CYP4F2 are relevant to it but were never
measured, so there is nothing to show for them.
This is not a defect against AC4, which says each card shows "its own primary gene's figure and no other" - showing
NUDT15 beside TPMT would fail AC4 as written. It is a limit of the design the plan pre-committed to, recorded here
rather than fixed silently, and it is a decision for the owner: leave the panel keyed on the primary gene, or widen it
to a drug's measured relevant genes (which needs AC4 amended before any code).
The Flutter suite now pins the fact rather than leaving it implicit: a test asserts every capability's primary gene is
exercised by some fixture, so the gap is visible if the registry changes.

